  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of initial Alaska Medicaid HCV DAA PA Clinical Criteria for Use, All Genotypes. Changes Approved 11/19/2021; Effective DOS 1/4/2022 and thereafter; Revised 5/5/2022. Revision history lists PDL update effective 6/1/2022.",
    "PDL preferred regimens in Tables 1a/1b do not require PA when prescribed consistently with the PDL. This pack covers non-preferred / PA-required DAA requests. Refer to Tables 1a/1b (including Mavyret and sofosbuvir/velpatasvir authorized generic) and Table 2 special conditions; product, genotype, cirrhosis and treatment-history table rows are not hard predicates.",
    "Quantity (notes only): do not exceed FDA-approved dose per day and duration.",
    "Renewal (notes only): regimens longer than 16 weeks may require timely submission of week-4 HCV RNA, which must be <25 IU/mL. Maintain chart documentation of week-4 RNA and SVR12 and make available on request. No extension without clinical evidence of benefit/effectiveness or for non-compliance; no extension or reauthorization for dispensing error (pharmacy must rectify at no cost to Medicaid or patient); no lost/stolen replacement.",
    "Ribavirin combination treatment is contraindicated in women who are pregnant or may become pregnant and men whose female partners are pregnant due to birth defects and fetal death risks. Ongoing patient engagement is encouraged to reduce resistance and reinfection.",
    "Incomplete requests: prescribers have 7 calendar days to supply additional information before non-clinical denial; re-review requires a new complete PA request.",
    "Age gate follows approval criterion 3: age >=12 or age >=3 and <12 with liver disease specialist directly or in consultation. Denial criterion 8 says ages 3 to 12; this boundary wording and Table 2 youth specialty guidance remain for manual review.",
    "Twin slug hepatitis-c-direct-acting-antivirals-for-chronic-hepatitis-c-criteria-all-produc shares this PDF and remains separately unencoded."
  ],
